sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch08-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because many domestic animals are believed to descend from two or more distinct species that are now fully fertile together, sterility between species is not indelible but can be removed by domestication.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hybrid sterility can be removed under domestication";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter VIII, “Hybridism”; section “Sterility various in degree, not universal, affected by close interbreeding, removed by domestication”. Scope: domestic animals derived from several wild species (dogs, cattle)"
}
